# DTO and Domain Design

DTO conventions:
- use immutable transport shapes (records when suitable)
- keep request/response DTOs separate from domain entities
- apply bean validation at transport boundary

Domain conventions:
- domain entities/value objects enforce business invariants
- do not expose persistence entities as API contracts

Mapping discipline:
- nested required fields must be mapped explicitly
- avoid ID-only shortcuts when full object context is required
- keep domain language consistent across use-case boundaries
